Sorry, but I think I did not understand your question.

>From what I understood, you want to compare the intercepts from group 1 and 2. If scalar invariance holds, then I assume the intercept difference for all items is statistically zero.
But in your syntax, you are comparing the intercept of item 2 with the intercept of item 3 within the same group. I do not know why you would be interested in this, but it simply means that the intercept of item 3 is 4.860 measurement units smaller than intercept of item 2, and this difference is statistically different from zero.

Best,
Yago

