Hello,

I am trying to figure out how to specify a simple latent variable model for ranking data in lavaan based on Maydeu-Olivares and Bockenholt, 2005 <http://10.1037/1082-989X.10.3.285>. I am wondering if I am missing some constraints or some scaling factors because the mean structure doesn’t match what I am expecting. Here are the details:
Simulations

I first simulated some latent utilities from independent normals with unique means and variances equal to 1. I then converted these to ranks based on the order statistics. From there, I created ordered indicators based on pairs. That is, if item 1 is ranked ahead of item 2, the indicator i1i2 gets a 1, and zero otherwise.
set.seed(5663) mu <- c(-4, -2, -1, 0) ranks <- sapply( 1:100, function(x){ s <- rnorm(length(mu), mean = mu) return(order(s)) } ) |> t() # give names colnames(ranks) <- paste0("i", 1:4) # create indexes indexes <- list() for(i in 1:(ncol(ranks) - 1)){ for(j in (i+1):ncol(ranks)){ indexes <- c( indexes, list(c(i, j)) ) } } # convert to pairs data pairs_dat <- matrix(0, nrow = nrow(ranks), ncol = choose(ncol(ranks), 2)) for(i in 1:nrow(pairs_dat)){ for(j in 1:ncol(pairs_dat)){ if(ranks[i, indexes[[j]][1]] < ranks[i, indexes[[j]][2]]){ pairs_dat[i, j] <- 1 } } } # give better names colnames(pairs_dat) <- c("i1i2", "i1i3", "i1i4", "i2i3", "i2i4", "i3i4") pairs_dat <- as.data.frame(pairs_dat)  Fitting the model

Based on the simple case 5 model, I constrain the latent variables to have variances of 1 and to be orthogonal. I also specify a mean structure, and constrain one of the latent means to zero for identifiability. I also want to specify that the indicators are observed without error since the ranks data are intransitive and imply a specific order. Here is the model specification.
# specify model components reg <- ' i1 ~ 1 i2 ~ 1 i3 ~ 1 i4 ~ 0 * 1 ' # fix the factor loadings as pairwise differences meas <- ' i1 =~ 1 * i1i2 + 1 * i1i3 + 1 * i1i4 i2 =~ -1 * i1i2 + 1 * i2i3 + 1 * i2i4 i3 =~ -1 * i1i3 + -1 * i2i3 + 1 * i3i4 i4 =~ -1 * i1i4 + -1 * i2i4 + -1 * i3i4 ' covars <- ' # residual variances constrained i1i2 ~~ 0 * i1i2 i1i3 ~~ 0 * i1i3 i1i4 ~~ 0 * i1i4 i2i3 ~~ 0 * i2i3 i2i4 ~~ 0 * i2i4 i3i4 ~~ 0 * i3i4 ' # fit the model mfit <- lavaan( model = c(reg, meas, covars), data = pairs_dat, ordered = names(pairs_dat)[1:6], parameterization = "theta", meanstructure = T, orthogonal = T, std.lv <http://std.lv> = T ) summary(mfit)  lavaan 0.6-18 ended normally after 10 iterations Estimator DWLS Optimization method NLMINB Number of model parameters 3 Number of observations 100 Model Test User Model: Standard Scaled Test Statistic 36.119 30.665 Degrees of freedom 18 18 P-value (Chi-square) 0.007 0.031 Scaling correction factor 1.513 Shift parameter 6.788 simple second-order correction Parameter Estimates: Parameterization Theta Standard errors Robust.sem Information Expected Information saturated (h1) model Unstructured Latent Variables: Estimate Std.Err z-value P(>|z|) i1 =~ i1i2 1.000 i1i3 1.000 i1i4 1.000 i2 =~ i1i2 -1.000 i2i3 1.000 i2i4 1.000 i3 =~ i1i3 -1.000 i2i3 -1.000 i3i4 1.000 i4 =~ i1i4 -1.000 i2i4 -1.000 i3i4 -1.000 Intercepts: Estimate Std.Err z-value P(>|z|) i1 0.942 0.226 4.170 0.000 i2 0.632 0.202 3.132 0.002 i3 0.365 0.178 2.051 0.040 i4 0.000 Thresholds: Estimate Std.Err z-value P(>|z|) i1i2|t1 -0.772 i1i3|t1 -1.341 i1i4|t1 -2.326 i2i3|t1 -0.739 i2i4|t1 -1.405 i3i4|t1 -0.954 Variances: Estimate Std.Err z-value P(>|z|) .i1i2 0.000 .i1i3 0.000 .i1i4 0.000 .i2i3 0.000 .i2i4 0.000 .i3i4 0.000 i1 1.000 i2 1.000 i3 1.000 i4 1.000 Scales y*: Estimate Std.Err z-value P(>|z|) i1i2 0.707 i1i3 0.707 i1i4 0.707 i2i3 0.707 i2i4 0.707 i3i4 0.707

The resulting summary of the model looks mostly as expected, but I haven’t been able to figure out why the latent means aren’t anywhere near the means I specified in the simulation. I also can’t figure out how to get from the estimated means to the thresholds. My understanding was that the threshold relationship should be

where  is a diagonal matrix with 1/sqrt(2) in the diagonals, based on the factor loadings matrix  and the specified covariance of the latent variables, which is just the identity matrix. What is happening under the hood to estimate the means and how do I get from the means to the thresholds? The thresholds seem right based on some post-hoc inspection, but I haven’t figured out how to recover the original means (or at least the spacing among them).
mean(pairs_dat$i1i2) # first threshold looks good 1- pnorm(-0.772)

