Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

> I think the problem is how to define the 'b2' parameter in the lavaan syntax.

Correct, you are not defining it correctly.  There is not NEW operator in lavaan, like there is in Mplus, but you can create one as the mean of an arbitrary "phantom construct" that is measured by nothing (and whose (co)variances are all 0).  See this old post:

https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/_-4zClO8oj8/m/wT3gaK_sBgAJ

ph =~ 0
ph ~ NA*1 + label("b2")*1 + 1?1 # free it, label it, start it at 1

b2 > 0.5 # constrain it to be > 0.5

## constrain loadings (do not "define" them with := operator)
  lambda11 == 1 - exp(-b2 * 1)
  lambda21 == 1 - exp(-b2 * 2)
  lambda31 == 1 - exp(-b2 * 3)
  lambda41 == 1 - exp(-b2 * 4)
  lambda51 == 1 - exp(-b2 * 5)
  lambda61 == 1 - exp(-b2 * 6)

Terrence D. Jorgensen    (he, him, his)
Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics
Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam
http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen

